  "notes_for_reviewer": "Official rekrutacja.pwr.edu.pl payments page (\"English-taught programmes, 2026/27, students admitted in 2026/27\") and the official Prospectus 2026/27 read 2026-10-25. Tuition is in PLN per semester (the page gives no annual totals and says the amount is unchanged for the whole study period); it is stored for international students as period semester. Bachelor: duration, English and the October 2026 start are from the prospectus (7 semesters = 3.5 years, 6 = 3). Master: the duration differs between tracks (3 or 4 semesters, different by intake and double-degree tracks), so it is NOT stored; the fee page lists one fee per field, and the master programmes of one field (for example the many Mining and Geology specialisations and the double degrees) are therefore merged into one programme per field. Fields with a different fee per intake (MONABIPHOT, Biosciences, Chemical Engineering and Technology) are stored as two programmes, one per intake. No application deadline dates, application fee (the 2024/25 table showed EUR 20 = PLN 85; not stored) or language-level requirements are on the pages used; the documents list is a standard guess and should be checked. Doctoral studies are tuition-free (page of the admission section) and are not collected."
